# Cloudflare Pages cache rules.
#
# KEEP THIS FILE NARROW. Pages MERGES every matching rule rather than letting
# the most specific one win, so a broad `/*` block leaks its headers onto the
# hashed bundles too — see BUG-HISTORY "Cloudflare Pages `_headers` over-broad".
# Add EXACT paths, not wildcards, unless you have verified the merge on a
# preview deploy first.
#
# index.html is the entry that points at the hashed bundles — always
# revalidate so a new deploy reaches the user on the next refresh.
# /assets/* are content-hashed by Vite, so a year-long immutable cache
# is correct: the filename itself changes whenever the contents change.

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# The service worker decides which shell every installed client runs, and the
# only lever we have to move a client stuck on a stale shell is bumping the
# VERSION constant inside this file — which is why it already carries thirteen
# one-shot purge bumps. That lever only works if the browser actually re-reads
# the file, so it must never be served from cache. Exact path, no wildcard, so
# it cannot merge onto anything else.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# /assets2/ then /assets3/ replaced /assets/ on 2026-07-31 (edge-poison
# outage — see vite.config.ts build.assetsDir).
#
# ⚠️ NO `immutable`, SHORT max-age — deliberately, and do not "optimise" it
# back. Cloudflare Pages answers an unknown path with index.html at 200, so a
# request that lands MID-DEPLOY (before the new hashed file propagates) gets
# HTML — and the edge then caches that HTML *under the asset URL* with whatever
# this rule says. With `max-age=31536000, immutable` that poisoned entry is
# pinned for a YEAR: on 2026-07-31 it took the whole ERP down (every route
# importing a poisoned chunk failed; no SW purge, VERSION bump or asset
# rename could clear it, because the bad copy lived at the edge). A 5-minute
# TTL bounds any repeat to minutes and self-heals with no deploy. The files are
# content-hashed, so a short TTL costs only cheap revalidations, never
# staleness.
/assets2/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

/assets3/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300

# Self-hosted web fonts. The woff2 files are fixed upstream builds and the
# names never get reused, so a year-long immutable cache is correct — same
# contract as /assets/*. The stylesheet sits under this rule too: any change to
# the font set must ship as a NEW file name + repointed link in index.html,
# never an in-place edit, or returning browsers will keep the old sheet for a
# year. That is why it is fonts-v2.css as of 2026-08-01 — an 800 face was added
# for IBM Plex Sans and the owner required it reach EVERY user, not only first
# visits. Next change: fonts-v3.css. Exact prefix, no overlap with the rules
# above, so nothing merges (see the warning at the top of this file).
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
